[ARCHITECT] 2026-06-27T00:00:00Z — Starting Architect step for Issue #29

Analysis:
- Feature requires unified benchmark harness and regression gate
- Need to measure render time, update time, memory, worker load, interaction latency
- Key risk: noisy measurements and optimizing the test instead of the product
- Must have reproducible benchmarks with clear thresholds

Decisions:
1. ADR-1: Statistical comparison over absolute thresholds — accounts for variance
2. ADR-2: Dedicated test dataset over live data — reproducibility
3. ADR-3: Warmup runs to reduce noise — stabilize JIT/cache
4. ADR-4: Markdown reports with ASCII trend charts — PR-compatible

Alternatives considered:
- Absolute threshold gates: Rejected — too noisy in CI
- Live data datasets: Rejected — not reproducible
- No warmup: Rejected — first runs not representative
- HTML dashboard: Rejected — external dependency

